title: BBEG
---

//Setting up the scene
//<<ChangeLocation DialogueSignals "Hallway">> -----> Player should already be in the hallway, so there's no need to set this

//<<SetCharacterLocation DialogueSignals "BBEG" "Hallway">> ----> Same as the other one

<<declare $Boss = "Zoe">> //There were some issues popping up with inconsistent naming, as well as the use of [BOSS] in the script, so I've declared a name to be used here. The name here has to be the same as the name set on the character node

?: So. You must be {$name}?
-> {$name}: Yes?
        ?: Are you sure? You don't seem certain.
        {$name}: No, I am. That's me. And, uh, you are?
        <<jump intro>>
-> {$name}: No?
        //<<jump no>> //TODO node "no" doesn't exist, but there's dialogue after so there's no need to jump to anything here, with the jump to sit just after
        {$Boss}: No? Are you sure? I do make a habit of knowing who my employees are.
        {$name}: I meant yes, sorry. Yes, that's me. Sorry Ms {$Boss}
        <<jump sit>>
-> {$name}: Who's asking?
        <<jump intro>>
-> {$name}: Who's that?
        {$Boss}: Who? It's... you? 
        {$name}: Uh right. Yes. Sorry, Ms {$Boss}. I am {$name}.
        <<jump sit>>

===
title: intro
---
{$Boss}: My name is {$Boss}. I am the current head of the Orion Institute.
{$name}: I. Yes, I knew that. Um. Nice to meet you.
        <<jump sit>>
===
title: sit
---
{$Boss}: So, {$name}, would you like to have a seat? I know this isn't as formal as an office, but I see no reason we can't be comfortable.
-> have a seat
        <<jump seat>>
-> decline
        <<jump stand>>
===
title: seat
---
{$name}: Sure, I'll sit.
{$name}: So, uh, what's up?
{$Boss}: What's up?
{$name}: Sorry, I meant, how can I help you?
{$Boss}: You seem quite nervous. Is everything alright?
-> tell the truth
        <<jump nervous>>
-> pretend all is good
        <<jump pretend>>
===
title: stand
---
{$name}: I'm all good, uh thanks.
{$Boss}: Suit yourself.
{$name}: So like, what can I help you with?
{$name}: Ma'am.
{$Boss}: You seem quite nervous. Is everything alright?
-> tell the truth
        <<jump nervous>>
-> pretend all is good
        <<jump pretend>>
===
title: nervous
---
{$name}: Well, it's not every day the, uh, 'big boss', comes all the way down to security to talk to a singular officer. You know?
{$Boss}: Ah I see. Honestly, I would probably be nervous too.
{$name}: Really?
{$Boss}: Of course! With no context, no time to mentally prepare? This would definitely be a nervewracking experience. 
{$Boss}: But rest assured, I'm not here to terrify you. I'm here to ask a favour.
{$name}: A favour? YOU want a favour? From me?
        <<jump favour>>
===
title: pretend
---
{$name}: Me? Nervous? Nah, just, uhm, stoked to get the opportunity to talk to you.
{$Boss}: Oh, uh, thank you {$name}. That's very kind. 
{$name}: Oh hey, any time. 
{$name}: So what do I get the pleasure of helping you with.
{$Boss}: I'm here to ask for a favour.
{$name}: A favour?
        <<jump favour>>
===
title: favour
---
{$Boss}: I've heard that you've been spending a bit of time talking to our newest, uh, 'guest'.
{$name}: Who, Cherry?
{$Boss}: Cherry? Is that her name?
{$name}: Um, I think so. It might be a nickname, I'm not sure. It's the name she gave me.
{$Boss}: How intriguing.
{$Boss}: She's not been very forthcoming with information so far. I, and a few others, have failed to get any information out of her so far. 
{$name}: Really?
{$Boss}: So I was wondering if you would talk to her, try and find out some information about her, and her species. I know it's technically outside your job duties, but I will discuss that with your Team Lead. 
{$Boss}: It's important that we find out as much as we can about her, and you seem to be our best option.
{$Boss}: So, what do you say, {$name}?
-> accept
        <<jump accept>>
-> decline
        <<jump decline>>

===
title: accept
---
{$name}: I would be happy to help. 
{$Boss}: Amazing! Thank you very much. You have no idea how much time and effort you will be saving me.
{$name}: Hey, any time. That's what I'm here for.
{$Boss}: Excellent. I'll send you some notes on the exact type of information we're looking for, so you know how best to direct the conversation. 
{$Boss}: Has she told you much about who she is?
-> tell the truth
        <<jump truth>>
-> lie
        <<jump lie>>
===
title: decline
---
{$name}: I'm... sorry, I don't really feel comfortable doing that. I'm not trained, and it's not like Cherry and I get along or anything, we've just had some mild conversations.
{$Boss}: Well that is disappointing, to say the least.
{$name}: I really am sorry.
{$Boss}: It's alright, it was a big ask in the first place. Just thought it was worth a shot.
{$Boss}: I will, of course, have to take this into consideration when conversations come up about furthering your career at the institute and whatnot.
{$Boss}: But maybe you can still help me. Has she told you much about her or her species?
-> tell the truth
        <<jump truth>>
-> lie
        <<jump lie>>
===
title: truth
---
{$name}: She has told me a couple of things.
{$Boss}: Oh? Such as?
{$name}: Well, she doesn't remember much. She appears to have almost total amnesia from before she got here.
{$Boss}: Including the explosion?
{$name}: Yeah. She just remembers it being cold.
{$name}: She seems to quite like clothes, but don't mention her hair. That's a touchy subject.
{$Boss}: Interesting. Anything else?
{$name}: Um. She doesn't seem to know if she has friends or family who would be looking for her.
{$Boss}: Hm. I wouldn't think she does.
{$name}: What do you mean?
{$Boss}: Oh nothing. Don't worry about it.
{$Boss}: Well thank you for your help. This has proven to be a very educational chat.
        <<jump goodbye>>
===
title: lie
---
{$name}: Uh, no, not really. We haven't spoken very much about her. She's mostly asked me questions.
{$Boss}: Well, although not helpful, this is still interesting, thank you.
{$name}: Sorry I couldn't be more helpful.
{$Boss}: Hey, this is technically out of your job description, so you've done your best.
        <<jump goodbye>>
===
title: goodbye
---
{$Boss}: I best get going. The duties of a director are endless, I'm afraid.
{$Boss}: Thank you {$name}, for meeting with me.
{$name}: That's all good. I guess I better get back to work myself.
{$Boss}: A word of advice, {$name}?
{$Boss}: Be careful of Cherry, and what you tell her. There is much more to her then meets the eye, and I can guarantee she hasn't been entirely honest with you.
{$name}: Uh, thanks. I'll keep that in mind.
{$Boss}: Goodbye {$name}. Take care.
{$name}: You too, ma'am.

<<jump EndDay>>
===